# Every output baseline, at whatever depth it sits. They are the bytes the
# emitter wrote, so a formatter must never touch one. Reformatting a baseline
# would silently rewrite the only thing those tests are guarding.
#
# The pattern is deliberately wider than the one directory that holds them
# today. A baseline that moves to another directory keeps its protection, and
# the move is the moment the protection is easiest to forget.
test/**/__snapshots__/
